Writer: Word EQ fields open as formulas

DOCX import read only EQ's \o, \s\do and ruby forms; every other
EQ field, such as \f(a,b) for a fraction, vanished (Gitea #9).
The import now turns an EQ field into a Math object through
the parser of the previous patch. Each command character keeps
its run's italic and vertAlign, as Word draws them (a with a
subscript 10 is a_{10}); the formula takes the field's font
size. A command the parser cannot read shows its field code as
text, so nothing vanishes and the failure stays visible. Only a
whole plain \s\do N(text) field stays lowered text, as before;
the old reader dropped anything after its first bracket.

